# Frozen research datasets are addressed BYTE-FOR-BYTE by the SHA-256 digests
# in manifest.json. Git must not normalize their line endings: this repo has
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows, so without -text Git would store LF in the
# blob and checkout LF on Linux/macOS CI runners, making every on-disk hash
# check fail (the generator wrote CRLF on Windows).
#
# This is a data-integrity rule, not a formatting preference: the committed
# dataset + manifest pair is the reproducibility evidence for all three
# domains' experiments. Regenerating datasets rewrites the manifest too.
*.csv -text
manifest.json -text
config.yaml -text
